{"availability":"available","full":"ASK-03/SnapSort","name":"SnapSort","description":"SnapSort is a cross-platform desktop application for offline, face-based image sorting and viewing.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":9,"forks":0,"created":"2025-05-14T10:56:50Z","updated":"2026-10-01T15:52:33Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://snapsort-website.vercel.app","topics":["clip-embeddings","cross-platform","electron-app","face-detection","faiss","image-viewer","onnxruntime","text-to-image-search"],"demo":"https://snapsort-website.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T17:54:44.848Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T17:54:44.848Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T17:54:44.848Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T17:54:44.848Z","stars":9,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["SnapSort is an open-source, cross-platform desktop application for offline, AI-powered image sorting, semantic searching, and face tagging. Select a folder of photos and instantly browse thumbnails; in the background, SnapSort will detect faces, extract semantic text-to-image embeddings, build a searchable embedding index, and let you:","Everything runs locally—no cloud uploads. SnapSort uses an Electron + React (TypeScript) frontend and a Python backend (FastAPI) utilizing onnxruntime with OpenCV (YuNet + SFace + CLIP) for machine learning, SQLite for metadata, and Faiss for fast vector search.","📌 Want to see what's coming next? Check out the todo.md for upcoming features, fixes, and improvements."],"features":["Search for photos by typing descriptions (e.g., \"tree in sunset\", \"group of people outdoors\").","Search for photos by typing a specific person's name (e.g., \"Rahul hiking\").","Merge multiple occurrences of the same person.","Instant Thumbnail Gallery: Loads and displays all images in a selected folder immediately, with a masonry layout.","Background AI Processing: Uses multiprocessi